WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.480
At long last, the first full trailer for Venom
has arrived.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.730
The film, which focuses on Tom Hardy as journalist
Eddie Brock, is the second big-screen appearance

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.050
of every comic fan's favorite alien symbiote.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.289
After the first brief teaser of the film conveyed
more about the tone of Venom than its actual

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:23.220
content, fans finally have their first real
look at what this movie will be about, and,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.859
more importantly, what Venom's iconic costume
is going to look like this time around.

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:32.861
The Venom trailer shows us glimpses of Hardy's
Brock, the villainous Life Foundation, and

00:00:32.861 --> 00:00:33.890
plenty more.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.260
Amid the explosions, alien symbiote attacks,
and sinister narration, there are a number

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.239
of key plot points and details the trailer
offers that you might've missed the first

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:44.239
time around.

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:48.050
Here are some of the small details you may
have missed in the Venom trailer.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.620
A lethal protector

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.070
There aren't a ton of great comics that depict
Venom as a hero.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.420
The most notable recent ones don't even feature
Eddie Brock in the starring role.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.110
As such, there are only so many Venom comics
from which the film could draw inspiration,

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.631
and from the trailer, it looks like the film
will be a loose adaptation of Venom: Lethal

00:01:06.631 --> 00:01:07.939
Protector.

00:01:07.939 --> 00:01:13.390
The '90s miniseries sees Venom and Eddie relocating
to San Francisco as fugitives from Spider-Man

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.390
and the authorities.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.689
They do so under an agreement that, as long
as they don't hurt anyone and stay out of

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:22.000
Spidey's business, Spider-Man will stay out
of theirs.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.240
The book features them taking on Carlton Drake
and the LIFE Foundation, both of which appear

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.719
in the trailer.

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:29.780
Voice of the people

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:33.200
Fans of the character may find themselves
pleasantly surprised by the direction in which

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.600
Venom takes Eddie Brock when it comes to his
career choice.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.340
The prior big screen incarnation of the character
from Spider-Man 3 depicts Eddie Brock as a

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.350
photographer, and a pretty skeevy one at that.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.830
From the looks of it, Venom will set Brock
on a different path, one with ties to some

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.409
of the character's best comic appearances.

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:55.899
The Eddie Brock we'll get in the film looks
to be an investigative journalist, a career

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:59.590
the character had in the original Spider-Man
comics where he first appeared.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.299
The Venom: Lethal Protector comic series further
establishes Brock as having been inspired

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:09.730
by journalistic coverage of the Watergate
scandal, which gave Brock an underlying anti-authoritarian

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.420
streak that could translate to film very well.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.440
It's a smart decision for a version of Venom
that looks to be more anti-hero than supervillain.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.750
As an investigative journalist, Brock should
have a strong sense of right and wrong.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:25.750
And we get a look at his willingness to make
bad people uncomfortable in the name of the

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.810
truth in the Venom trailer.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.100
It's a great character decision and bodes
well for Brock as a likeable protagonist.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.120
A dapper villain

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:39.340
The Venom trailer also gives us our first
real look at the film's villain: Carlton Drake,

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.250
played by Riz Ahmed.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:46.150
Drake is another carryover from Lethal Protector,
albeit one with which the filmmakers seem

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.860
to have taken a few liberties.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.760
In the comics, Drake is an older man running
the Life Foundation.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.500
He's a shady dude, but he's not responsible
for Venom and Eddie's bonding, nor for the

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.840
discovery of the original symbiote, although
he does discover the existence of others.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.780
It looks like Ahmed's take on the character
will be significantly different.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.940
Ahmed is young and attractive, and, by the
looks of it, he'll be a prominent media figure

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.610
in the world of the film.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:16.450
He's also far more directly tied to the symbiotes'
presence on Earth, with his Life Foundation

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:20.980
seeming to be responsible for either discovering
the symbiotes or bringing them to Earth to

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.020
begin with.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.060
It makes for a villain far more directly tied
to the protagonist, and that's likely going

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.520
to be a good thing.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.180
Love is in the air

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.720
We get our first look at the dynamic between
Tom Hardy's Eddie Brock and Michelle Williams'

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.390
Anne Weying in the Venom trailer as well.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:40.660
In the comics, Weying is Brock's ex-wife,
even though they appear to be together in

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.920
this cinematic take.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.810
Their relationship may still be a bit complicated,
since in the comics she also eventually gets

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.830
a symbiote of her own and becomes the villainous
She-Venom.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.840
With multiple symbiotes at play in the film,
let's not rule out an appearance from that

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.300
particular alter-ego just yet.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.040
A complicated relationship

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.730
The relationship between a host and a symbiote
in Marvel comics isn't necessarily defined

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:08.700
by a strict set of rules, but generally speaking,
there's usually a decision made on the part

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.010
of the host to bond with it.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.150
"Why would we do that?"

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:18.120
Here, it's not clear how much of a choice
Eddie Brock has about sharing his body.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.460
Eddie doesn't even seem to understand what's
happening to him during the bonding process.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.470
And when his Venom powers are finally unleashed
on the men who come to his apartment looking

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:31.150
for their boss's "property," he seems just
as shocked by what happens as they are.

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:35.439
It's a pretty cool storytelling choice, one
that opens up possible explorations of body

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.020
horror and Eddie's loss of autonomy as the
host, cemented by the symbiote's chilling

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:40.540
line:

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.460
"We can do whatever we want.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:44.820
Do we have a deal?"

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:49.909
So, Venom will not only have a mind of his
own in the film, but also a voice.

00:04:49.909 --> 00:04:52.300
We hear him speaking to Eddie in the trailer.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:56.280
Since there are obviously two distinct and
separate characters that happen to occupy

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:01.060
the same body, we're all in for the inevitable
struggle for control and dominance between

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.139
the two.

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:04.240
One giant leap for mankind

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.259
The Venom symbiote origin story of the comics
is a little bit complicated, but basically

00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:13.639
Spider-Man finds the Venom symbiote while
he's in another dimension, fighting in the

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:17.100
Beyonder's Secret Wars with the rest of the
Marvel Universe.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.599
And since Peter Parker's being shared between
Marvel and Sony, it looks like Venom is going

00:05:21.599 --> 00:05:25.419
to cook up its own, streamlined origin story
instead.

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:30.689
The Venom trailer seems to reveal that, rather
than Eddie discovering Venom through Spider-Man,

00:05:30.689 --> 00:05:32.600
the Life Foundation does.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:37.300
It also skips the element of Venom's origin
where it masquerades as a superhero suit.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:42.080
The alien that the foundation discovers is
in pure symbiote form.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.910
There appears to be no intended trickery on
its part.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:50.949
The audience, and the film's characters, will
see it in its true, goopy form from the start.

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:53.740
And a goopy Venom is a happy Venom!

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.740
Thanks for watching!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.349
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:57.349 --> 00:05:59.440
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

